 agent that asked[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Every sase gate that an agent creates becomes a named gate shell in[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]that agent's family, kills its creator instead of blocking it, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]streams its approved commands' live output into ACE, owns the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]family's TALE/QUESTION/APPROVED statuses, and launches a [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]configurable follow-up agent carrying the gate's typed results — [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]with gates and monitors sharing one family-shell substrate.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]14[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]10[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]gate_shells.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/gate_shells.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-ud[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-ud/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bounded gate response lock[/bold #D7AFFF]                                    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]lock-timeout[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]lock-timeout: give file_lock an optional timeout and use it in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]cancel_gate so a cancellation can never block behind an approved [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]long-running command.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The sase.shells family-shell substrate[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]shells[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]shells: extract member creation, suffix allocation, handoff, settlement,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]follow-up launch, prompt scaffolding, status pairs, and state buckets [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]out of sase.monitor into a kind-parameterized sase.shells package, with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase.monitor as a facade; migrate monitor follow-ups to #fork:<family>.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Gate shell creation, handoff, and settlement[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]gate-shell[dim] · [dim][/dim]after shells[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate-shell: add the additive `shell` block to the v3 gate request, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]create the gate-shell family member with promotion and claim transfer, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]hand off and kill the creator through .sase_gate_pending, run the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ordered settlement, short-circuit %auto, and bound pending gate shells [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with a required timeout and a reclaim chop.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust read-side gate shell rules[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]gate-core-rs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gate-shell[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate-core-rs: add the flat gate fields to AgentMetaWire and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]DoneMarkerWire, add is_real_gate_member_record, free the runner slot for[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]a pending gate shell in both the Rust and Python admission copies, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]extend the scanner and newest-family-shell selection.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Durable gate execution and live output[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]gate-exec[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gate-shell[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate-exec: bind the executor's three streaming callbacks to the gate [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]shell's gate.log through the shared bounded writer, add `sase gate [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]answer --detach` and default shell gates to it, record the running [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]command's pid, and write the settle-time chat file.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Gate shells in ACE[/bold #D7AFFF]                                            [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]gate-tui[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gate-core-rs, gate-exec[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate-tui: add the ⋔ gate glyph and legend entry, per-kind shell lanes [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and chips, the GATE sub-section of AGENT REPLY, the selected-gate-shell [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]live pane, fold registration, an individual decision at each of the ten [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]is_monitor filter sites, and PNG goldens.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Configurable per-branch follow-up[/bold #D7AFFF]                             [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]gate-followup[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gate-exec[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate-followup: implement the branch-keyed next map with prompt, output, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fork, model, status, and accent; the results/tail/file/none output [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]policy with results as the default; the reserved timeout/stopped/failed [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]keys; the workspace policy; and golden tests over every composed prompt.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fork, CLI, and conformance[/bold #D7AFFF]                                    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]gate-fork-cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gate-followup[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate-fork-cli: classify a settled gate shell in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]resolve_family_member_shell with a GATE SHELL source label, add `sase [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate list`/`show`/`cancel` as peers of the monitor verbs, grow the gate [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]conformance matrix a shell dimension, and rewrite the /sase_gate skill [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]template.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Migrate HITL and launch approval[/bold #D7AFFF]                              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]hitl-launch-migration[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gate-followup[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]hitl-launch-migration: convert workflow_hitl_gate and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]launch_request_response from blocking waits to shell gates with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]follow-ups, retiring two of the four wait_for_gate consumers.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Migrate /sase_questions[/bold #D7AFFF]                                      [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]questions-migration[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gate-followup, gate-fork-cli[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]questions-migration: make the question gate a gate shell behind the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]epic's beta flag, persist each Q&A round on its own gate shell instead [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]of LoopState RAM, and delete the blocking wait and in-process successor.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  11 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Migrate /sase_plan[/bold #D7AFFF]                                           [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]plan-migration[dim] · [dim][/dim]after questions-migration[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]plan-migration: make the tale and epic plan gates gate shells behind the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]same flag, launch the coder from the approve branch with the launch it [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]uses today, persist feedback rounds on gate shells, and delete [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]handle_plan_approval's wait loop.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  12 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Retire the --q asker suffix[/bold #D7AFFF]                                  [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]q-suffix-cleanup[dim] · [dim][/dim]after plan-migration[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]q-suffix-cleanup: delete PLAN_CHAIN_QUESTION_SUFFIX and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]root/phase-question suffix taxonomy now that the gate shell owns the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]question, leaving the asker as an ordinary agent shell.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  13 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Collapse the status machinery and remove the flag[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]status-collapse[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gate-tui, hitl-launch-migration, [/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#AF87FF][dim]q-suffix-cleanup[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]status-collapse: fold the flat monitor_* and gate_* wire blocks into one[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]nested family_shell record at wire schema v7, retire the notification [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]status overrides, family status predicates, synthetic planner children, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and colour-ladder branches after pinning their accents, and remove the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]beta flag.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  14 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Memory, decision record, and skills[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]memory-and-skills[dim] · [dim][/dim]after status-collapse[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]memory-and-skills: write the Gate Shell glossary strand and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]gates-never-block decision record, edit the Sase Shell, Proc Shell, Sase[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Gate, Sase Monitor, and Agent Family strands, run sase memory init, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]update the /sase_monitor, /sase_plan, and /sase_questions skill [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]templates.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-ud","llm